  "result": "Here's the draft (about 95 words). I haven't added it to `README.md` yet.\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nEach carrier has its own module in `shop/carriers/`, for example `shop/carriers/acme.py`.\nThere are 20 of them. All are registered in `REGISTRY` in `shop/carriers/__init__.py`,\nand you look one up by name with `shop.carriers.get(\"acme\")`.\n\nEvery carrier module defines a `BASE_RATE` in cents. This is a flat charge that is added\nbefore the weight charge and the zone multiplier (`local`, `regional`, `national`) are\napplied. `rate()` returns an integer number of cents.\n\nMost carriers take weight in kilograms (`PER_KG`, `MAX_KG`). **Maple is the exception:**\n`shop/carriers/maple.py` takes weight in **grams** (`PER_GRAMS`, `MAX_GRAMS`), so convert\nbefore you call `rate()`.\n```\n\nWhile reading the code I noticed that four carriers (`delta`, `kestrel`, `onyx`, `tundra`) have no `tracking_url()` method, unlike the rest. The draft doesn't mention it. If that's intentional, it might be worth a line in the README.\n\nShould I add this section to `README.md`?",
